WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.617
TIMESTAMPTZ is PostgreSQL's timestamp with time zone type.

00:00:04.617 --> 00:00:05.432
Conceptually, it represents an instant.

00:00:05.432 --> 00:00:08.922
PostgreSQL can display that instant in different time zones.

00:00:08.922 --> 00:00:14.022
This is useful for events collected across locations.

00:00:14.022 --> 00:00:19.052
The key distinction is between the stored instant and the clock representation shown to a user.

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:21.407
Choose temporal types based on meaning.

00:00:21.407 --> 00:00:24.077
DATE is for calendar dates without time of day.

00:00:24.077 --> 00:00:28.312
TIMESTAMP stores a date and time without a time-zone interpretation.

00:00:28.312 --> 00:00:32.942
TIMESTAMPTZ represents an instant in time and is usually safer for events that cross regions or

00:00:32.942 --> 00:00:34.856
daylight-saving changes.
